{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1795427824145081002,"compiled_state":{"alias":"limitless-defaceable-beaver","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"df4aa2975b31b0c2f9e835b55fed5e07e07d677572b8f893f2226035cd3f748c","event_uuid":"6c86d69e-bf78-42ed-a82d-b61d655204b0","position":{"commit_sha":"3c1b4b31b031dbcc61a3e823a04484acdc5b8fb4","position":"1795427803083318001-6c86d69e-bf78-42ed-a82d-b61d655204b0"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"9ce80d97149ff0cab719a4d0264ef73ba4b1a77377e4b5921245e43340726852","event_uuid":"8e1cc804-20e3-460a-b369-67c4da14bf57","position":{"commit_sha":"ae9cc80d76d845c41b57f651e5b7ff93c5a2fd12","position":"1795427824145081001-8e1cc804-20e3-460a-b369-67c4da14bf57"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1795427803083318001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"8e1cc804-20e3-460a-b369-67c4da14bf57","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"7c81-7bbf-8275-41b9"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nFound 2026-11-23 PST while fixing immoral-heated-doctorfish (Gerrit/Jira credentials in operator argv). `docs/mcp-client-setup.md` (lines 95 and 174) tells users to run `copilot mcp add ... --header \"Authorization: Bearer $MCP_CLIENT_PAT_COPILOT\"` and `claude mcp add ... --header \"Authorization: Bearer ${MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CLAUDE}\"`. The double quotes make the shell expand the PAT, so the rebar MCP client PAT is on the `copilot`/`claude` process command line while it runs, where any local user or process monitor can read it, and it is then written in clear into the client's config file.\n\nThis was kept out of immoral-heated-doctorfish because it is a different credential (the MCP client PAT, not a Gerrit or Jira credential) and the fix depends on each vendor CLI's handling of a literal `${VAR}` header placeholder, which needs checking against the Copilot CLI and Claude Code documentation.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `docs/mcp-client-setup.md` no longer shows a command that puts the expanded MCP client PAT in a process argv; the documented setup keeps the PAT out of argv (for example a literal `${VAR}` placeholder the client expands at connect time, verified against each client's documentation).\n- [ ] The operator-credential argv guard added by immoral-heated-doctorfish scans `docs/mcp-client-setup.md` and passes.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"672d-a44d-1c25-4b69","ticket_type":"bug","title":"MCP client setup docs put the PAT in argv","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["6c86d69e-bf78-42ed-a82d-b61d655204b0","8e1cc804-20e3-460a-b369-67c4da14bf57"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795427824145081002,"uuid":"8e0ba3ce-5854-4499-8633-598653f84a96"}